      "title": "Use the zeros of the factors",
      "body": "<p>Set each given linear factor equal to zero. Substitute those two inputs into the cubic, setting each result equal to zero.</p>",
      "recap": "A polynomial is zero at the zero of any of its factors.",
      "pitfall": "Solve the whole linear factor, including its coefficient of x.",
      "pause": "Write two equations in p and q.",
      "recall": [
