  "solution": "<p><strong>1. Use the factor theorem.</strong> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>q</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2. Eliminate p.</strong> Subtract the second equation from four times the first: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>15</mn><mi>q</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></math>. Hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>3. Evaluate the requested expression.</strong> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>26</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>22</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>Answer C.</strong> Substitution into the two factor equations provides a quick arithmetic check.</p>",
